# Project workflow

This rule is an example. Cursor does not load it from `ProjectWorkflow/cursor/`. It loads rules from `.cursor/rules/` at the repository root. Copying it there makes it apply while you are in the other VibeBash projects too, and it can fight the root `CLAUDE.md`. Leave it here until you mean to turn that on.

## When this rule is on

- The shared memory is `ProjectWorkflow/vault`. Start at `vault/Home.md` and the latest daily note's index.
- For a campaign, email, or ad brief, read the matching file in `vault/jobs/` and follow its links. Append the draft. Do not invent a new note per draft.
- For a code change, read `vault/jobs/Ship-Change/Ship-Change.md`. Edit the files the spec names. Show the diff.
- Before you finish, append one index line to today's file in `vault/daily/`. If you skip this, the next chat starts blank. That is the Cursor-specific failure.
- Do not put keys, customer lists, or billing exports in the vault. This repo is public.
- Fieldnote is fictional.

## How this place differs

Cursor is the better place to edit code while someone is watching the diff. It is a poor system of record. Obsidian and Claude Code keep the graph. Codex is the better place to run a job that is already fully specified and does not need you in the loop. A Cursor cloud agent sees git. It does not see an Obsidian vault that exists only on your computer.
